<SubpageLayout title="Naoero i emam · The People" description="Nauru people and community life: language, family, everyday culture and the social ties that shape the island." sectionEmoji="👥" sectionLabel="Emam i en" includeTopBar={true} includeFooter={true} locale="na">
  <p>The Nauruan people are a small island community with a strong sense of continuity, family ties and shared responsibility. Nauruan and English are the most important languages in everyday life.</p>
<h2>Language and community</h2>
<p>Nauruan is the national language; English is widely used in government, school and business. Family networks remain central, and community life is closely tied to church, school and local events.</p>
